{% doc %}
  Responsive grid of product cards (snippets/card-product) for collection and search
  listings. Columns come from custom properties that the section sets per instance:
  `--pg-cols-mobile` (1 or 2, below 768px), 3 from 768px, `--pg-cols-desktop` from
  1200px (styles: assets/section-main-collection.css). Rows are equal height; cards keep
  their image boxes, so nothing shifts while images load.

  The first `eager` cards load their images eagerly (the first row is above the fold);
  the rest are lazy. Items are direct children of the `[data-grid]` list, so a "load
  more" script can append the next page's `[data-grid] > li` into it.

  Pass only products (`search.results | where: 'object_type', 'product'` on search).

  `photos_first`: within the page, the products that have a photo come first, each group in the
  given order (most of the catalogue has no photo yet). Callers pass it only with an order that is
  not a price or date order: the category's default (manual, best-selling) or search relevance.
  The page holds the same products either way, so pagination and "load more" are unchanged.

  `rank`: search results only, the output of snippets/search-rank ("<steps>#<map>"): one pass per group in its
  order (the searched device first, then other products, accessories last), photos first inside each group when
  `photos_first` is set too.

  Sold out: left out, unless theme settings › מוצרים שאזלו "מוצרים שאזלו מוצגים באתר" is on; then they come after
  every available product of the page (each in the order above), so a page never shows one before an available one.
  `sold_out_only`: the category's sold-out part (sections/main-collection, filter.v.availability=0, whose results also
  hold products with one sold-out variant among available ones): only the products with nothing available.

  Classes: .product-grid, .product-grid__item.

  @param {object} products - Array of products for the current page.
  @param {string} section_id - The calling section's id (unique ids inside cards).
  @param {number} [eager] - How many cards load eagerly. Default 4.
  @param {string} [heading] - Tag of the card titles: 'h2', 'h3' (default) or 'h4'.
  @param {string} [id] - id of the list.
  @param {string} [label] - Accessible name of the list.
  @param {boolean} [photos_first] - Products with a photo first within the page. Default false.
  @param {string} [rank] - Search order groups from snippets/search-rank. Default none (the given order).
  @param {boolean} [sold_out_only] - Only products with nothing available (the category's sold-out part). Default false.

  @example
  {% render 'product-grid', products: collection.products, section_id: section.id, eager: 4, heading: 'h3' %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign pg_eager = eager | default: 4
  assign pg_heading = heading | default: 'h3'
  assign pg_passes = 1
  if photos_first
    assign pg_passes = 2
  endif
  assign pg_index = 0
  # Availability passes: the available products, then (the setting on) the sold-out ones.
  assign pg_avail = 'in' | split: ','
  if sold_out_only
    assign pg_avail = 'out' | split: ','
  elsif settings.sold_out_visible
    assign pg_avail = 'in,out' | split: ','
  endif
  assign pg_steps = 'all' | split: '|'
  assign pg_map = ''
  if rank != blank
    assign pg_rank_parts = rank | strip | split: '#'
    assign pg_steps = pg_rank_parts[0] | split: '|'
    assign pg_map = pg_rank_parts[1]
  endif
-%}
<ul
  class="product-grid"
  role="list"
  data-grid
  {% if id != blank %}
    id="{{ id }}"
  {% endif %}
  {% if label != blank %}
    aria-label="{{ label | escape }}"
  {% endif %}
>
  {%- for pg_avail_pass in pg_avail -%}
  {%- for pg_step in pg_steps -%}
  {%- for pg_pass in (1..pg_passes) -%}
    {%- for product in products -%}
      {%- liquid
        if pg_avail_pass == 'in' and product.available == false
          continue
        endif
        if pg_avail_pass == 'out' and product.available
          continue
        endif
        if pg_step != 'all'
          assign pg_key = ',' | append: product.id | append: '=' | append: pg_step | append: ','
          unless pg_map contains pg_key
            continue
          endunless
        endif
        if pg_passes == 2
          if pg_pass == 1 and product.featured_media == blank
            continue
          endif
          if pg_pass == 2 and product.featured_media != blank
            continue
          endif
        endif
        assign pg_index = pg_index | plus: 1
        assign pg_lazy = true
        if pg_index <= pg_eager
          assign pg_lazy = false
        endif
      -%}
      <li class="product-grid__item">
        {%- render 'card-product',
          product: product,
          lazy: pg_lazy,
          heading: pg_heading,
          section_id: section_id,
          show_swatches: settings.card_show_swatches
        -%}
      </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
</ul>
